{"timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:02:35.575Z","ordinal":17,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_70000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000022","call_id":"call_00000000000000000000000000000022","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[{\"name\":\"apply_patch\",\"description\":\"The `apply_patch` tool can be used to edit files. This is a FREEFORM tool, so do not wrap the patch in JSON.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { apply_patch(input: string): Promise<unknown>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__seamark__change_set\",\"description\":\"Pre-edit blast radius for planned files: what history says changes together with them (N/M commits: N shared, M counted in the mined window), who calls their symbols, which effects they can reach. It also prepares the pins and checks that apply; call it before you construct any change, also for one file or a new path, then construct the change in a later step, not in the same generated program. Preparation authorizes no write.\\n\\nSeamark answers questions that need history, co-change, lessons, or effect reach. Call change_set with the planned files before you construct any change, also for one file or a new path, and again when the file set grows: it prepares the pins and checks that apply. Construct the change in a later step, not in the same generated program; preparation authorizes no write. Call why for a load-bearing symbol you change; orient only when the repo or subsystem is unfamiliar; check on the diff with lesson_checks: true before reporting completion, with new files staged first because git diff HEAD skips them, and answer every file it lists under history suggests also reviewing; expand only for a ref you need. Co-change means usually changes together, not depends on. Missing or unindexed evidence never means safe. Read a known file or symbol directly; a typo, comment, or formatting edit needs no call.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__seamark__change_set(args: {\\n  // repo-relative paths you plan to edit or create\\n  files: Array<string>;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__seamark__check\",\"description\":\"Evaluate a unified diff's reachable effects against workspace policy (.seamark/policy.yaml). Omit diff to use `git diff HEAD`. Not read-only: it refreshes the index, appends to .seamark/audit.jsonl, writes a lessons-audit.jsonl firing record when it prints lessons, and with lesson_checks appends to lesson-check-audit.jsonl.\\n\\nSeamark answers questions that need history, co-change, lessons, or effect reach. Call change_set with the planned files before you construct any change, also for one file or a new path, and again when the file set grows: it prepares the pins and checks that apply. Construct the change in a later step, not in the same generated program; preparation authorizes no write. Call why for a load-bearing symbol you change; orient only when the repo or subsystem is unfamiliar; check on the diff with lesson_checks: true before reporting completion, with new files staged first because git diff HEAD skips them, and answer every file it lists under history suggests also reviewing; expand only for a ref you need. Co-change means usually changes together, not depends on. Missing or unindexed evidence never means safe. Read a known file or symbol directly; a typo, comment, or formatting edit needs no call.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__seamark__check(args: {\\n  // unified diff; optional\\n  diff?: string;\\n  // also verify the working tree against executable lesson checks (lesson-verification/1); default false\\n  lesson_checks?: boolean;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__seamark__expand\",\"description\":\"Progressive disclosure: turn a ref from another report into its content — a symbol, FQN, or file:start-end into source lines; lessons:<dir> into an area's raw review findings (one-offs included, for pattern-spotting).\\n\\nSeamark answers questions that need history, co-change, lessons, or effect reach. Call change_set with the planned files before you construct any change, also for one file or a new path, and again when the file set grows: it prepares the pins and checks that apply. Construct the change in a later step, not in the same generated program; preparation authorizes no write. Call why for a load-bearing symbol you change; orient only when the repo or subsystem is unfamiliar; check on the diff with lesson_checks: true before reporting completion, with new files staged first because git diff HEAD skips them, and answer every file it lists under history suggests also reviewing; expand only for a ref you need. Co-change means usually changes together, not depends on. Missing or unindexed evidence never means safe. Read a known file or symbol directly; a typo, comment, or formatting edit needs no call.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__seamark__expand(args: {\\n  // symbol name, FQN, file:start[-end], or lessons:<dir>\\n  ref: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__seamark__orient\",\"description\":\"One-screen repo overview: scale, modules, most-called API, files that change in groups, recent decisions. Call once when the repository or subsystem is unfamiliar.\\n\\nSeamark answers questions that need history, co-change, lessons, or effect reach. Call change_set with the planned files before you construct any change, also for one file or a new path, and again when the file set grows: it prepares the pins and checks that apply. Construct the change in a later step, not in the same generated program; preparation authorizes no write. Call why for a load-bearing symbol you change; orient only when the repo or subsystem is unfamiliar; check on the diff with lesson_checks: true before reporting completion, with new files staged first because git diff HEAD skips them, and answer every file it lists under history suggests also reviewing; expand only for a ref you need. Co-change means usually changes together, not depends on. Missing or unindexed evidence never means safe. Read a known file or symbol directly; a typo, comment, or formatting edit needs no call.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__seamark__orient(args: { [key: string]: unknown; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__seamark__why\",\"description\":\"Explain a symbol or file: definition, callers/callees with confidence origins, files that historically change with it (N/M commits: N shared, M counted in the mined window), commits that explain it.\\n\\nSeamark answers questions that need history, co-change, lessons, or effect reach. Call change_set with the planned files before you construct any change, also for one file or a new path, and again when the file set grows: it prepares the pins and checks that apply. Construct the change in a later step, not in the same generated program; preparation authorizes no write. Call why for a load-bearing symbol you change; orient only when the repo or subsystem is unfamiliar; check on the diff with lesson_checks: true before reporting completion, with new files staged first because git diff HEAD skips them, and answer every file it lists under history suggests also reviewing; expand only for a ref you need. Co-change means usually changes together, not depends on. Missing or unindexed evidence never means safe. Read a known file or symbol directly; a typo, comment, or formatting edit needs no call.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__seamark__why(args: {\\n  // symbol name, FQN, or repo-relative file path\\n  query: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000016","create_time":1794862955.575871}},"meta